Description: keyboard backlight and RGB lighting control for laptops
 ByteKeys controls the keyboard lighting of Linux laptops: white backlights
 as well as single-zone, multi-zone and per-key RGB keyboards. It detects the
 laptop and its keyboard automatically and configures itself.
 .
 Features: brightness, colors, zones and per-key colors; software and
 hardware effects; automation rules (dim on battery, off when idle, low
 battery and overheat warnings, Caps Lock indicator, schedules); profiles;
 a tray icon and a command line tool.
 .
 Hardware is reached through kernel drivers (asus-wmi, thinkpad_acpi,
 dell-laptop, system76_acpi, tuxedo-drivers and others), common USB lighting
 controllers, and OpenRGB. A small system service (bytekeysd) does the
 privileged work so the control panel runs as a normal user.
